# .vercelignore
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# This project has no build step and no output directory: Vercel serves the repo
# root directly as static files. That is convenient, but it also means anything
# committed is published at its own URL. Verified against production:
#
#   /migrations/001_hardening.sql   -> 200, byte-identical
#   /tests/check-pricing.mjs        -> 200, byte-identical
#   /tools/build-og-image.py        -> 200, byte-identical
#   /README-FIXES.md                -> 200
#
# None of that is a credential — the Supabase anon key is public by design, and
# every secret in this project lives in Vercel environment variables, which are
# never in the repo. So this is not an incident. It is still wrong: the database
# schema, the internal fix log and the test suite have no reason to be reachable
# from the open internet, and every file added to those folders is published by
# default unless someone remembers to think about it.
#
# DO NOT ADD 'package.json' OR 'package-lock.json'. Vercel needs them to install
# the runtime dependencies for the api/ functions (stripe,
# @supabase/supabase-js, @vercel/og). Excluding them breaks every endpoint.
#
# assets/, api/, *.html, og-image*.png, manifest.json, robots.txt, sitemap and
# the favicons MUST stay served — they are the actual website.

# Internal documentation and fix history.
README-FIXES.md
FUNNEL.md
FEATURE-ROADMAP.md

# Database schema. Not secret, but no reason to publish the shape of the
# customer tables.
migrations/

# Test suite. Publishing it also hands over exactly which invariants are
# enforced, which is free reconnaissance for anyone probing the checkout.
tests/

# Local build tooling. Nothing here runs in production; the social card it
# produces is already committed as a static PNG.
tools/

# Version control internals.
.git/
.gitignore
.vercelignore
